Report, receipts and the two OPTIONS-REGISTRY evidence cells for the code committed in a63edc326.

m=17408 n=512 k=5120, one binary, arms env-gated, 3 interleaved rounds, GGML_VK_PERF_LOGGER
dispatch time (r52b-evidence/20-perf-3arm.txt):

  A1 coopmat mul_mm, packed OFF   S-X8  58738 us (median of 59204/58738/58279)
  A2 coopmat mul_mm, packed ON    S-X8  57444 us (57444/57224/57522)   -2.20%, NON-OVERLAPPING
  A0 coopmat mul_mm control       q8_0  61651 us (63196/59694/61651)
  B  MMQ under coopmat            S-X8  90967 us  = +54.9% time, 1.55x SLOWER
  B  MMQ under coopmat            q8_0  72501 us  = +17.6% slower
  C  GGML_VK_DISABLE_COOPMAT=1    S-X8  91824 us  = same place as B, which is the dispatch receipt

HQ's third arm is answered and it is a refusal: integer MMQ under coopmat loses for BOTH types on
gfx1103, so the fix is the tile decode as briefed, not the routing. WI-1724 should be closed as
measured or re-scoped.

Two corrections to the lane's premises, both load-bearing:

- S-X8 mul_mm is FASTER than q8_0 at this shape (-6.8% after the fix, -4.7% before). The R48i 4B
  pp128 deficit is real but is not this shape's mul_mm; it stays open.
- The packed decode buys 2.2%, not the double-digit the VMEM accounting (16 -> 6 byte loads per
  8 weights, 8192 -> 3072 per BK step against 524,288 MACs) would predict if the decode were the
  ceiling. At this shape it is not; the coopmat tile schedule is.

Planted RED inside the SX8_PACKED_DECODE branch only (qh1 -> qh0, 4 of every 8 weights):
packed ON goes 16/17 with the new n=512 row FAIL at ERR 0.990118204 and the n=64 row 0/1, while all
sixteen n<=8 rows stay GREEN and the packed-OFF arm of the same binary stays 17/17. Dispatched,
switch-selected, and mul_mm proven reachable only at wide n. Restored with
`git checkout a63edc326 -- <file>`; git diff against that commit is empty, and the restored binary
is 17/17 + 1/1.

Correctness: 109/109 0 FAIL in both decode arms; 17/17 + 9/9 + 1/1 + 1/1 with MMQ under coopmat.
The full -o MUL_MAT sweep is OWED: three attempts died with host std::bad_alloc at
MUL_MAT(m=5120,n=1,k=17408) while three other makers held 6-16 GB each on a 31.7 GB one-pool box.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-243 R52b S-X8 coopmat mul_mm decode, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: diagnostic only (one shape, 3 interleaved rounds, receipts); HQ benches quiet
Lane: lane-243
